<title>PERU: Peru's Sept coffee output falls 40.7 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's Sept coffee output falls 40.7 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's September coffee production fell 40.7 percent to 586 tonnes, compared with the same month last year, the Agriculture Ministry said Monday.</p>
<p>Coffee output for the first nine months was up 11.2 percent to 107,049 tonnes, compared to the same period of 1995.</p>
<p>Non-decaffeinated coffee exports rose 14.5 percent in August to 16,923 tonnes, worth $37.2 million, while exports in the first eight months gained 35.6 percent to 71,147 tonnes, worth $157.5 million, the ministry said.</p>
<p>It did not give export figures for September.</p>
<p>Peru, whose principal coffee harvest is between April and November, is South America's number four producer after Brazil, Colombia and Ecuador, according to the government.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Cawthorne, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134</p>
</text>
